 ```
 
+`dokuwiki` produces [DokuWiki](https://www.dokuwiki.org/wiki:syntax#tables)
+tables with `^` separating header cells and `|` separating data cells, and
+no horizontal rules. Alignment uses at least two spaces on the opposite side
+of a cell (both sides for centered cells); decimal alignment is rendered as
+right alignment. Literal `|` and `^` characters in headers and data are escaped
+with DokuWiki's `%%...%%` syntax.
+
+```pycon
+>>> print(tabulate([["apple", 3]], ["name", "qty"], tablefmt="dokuwiki"))
+^ name    ^    qty ^
+| apple   |      3 |
+
+```
+
 `mediawiki` format produces a table markup used in
 [Wikipedia](http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Help:Tables) and on other
 MediaWiki-based sites:
